# Dawnhand Dissident's rulings: it "must be under your control in order for you to start casting a creature spell using its last
# ability, but it doesn't need to stay under your control throughout that process", and the creature spell keeps its own timing ("only
# during your main phase while the stack is empty"). Bot1 surveils its Walking Ballista into the graveyard and exiles it with the
# Dissident, blighting its two Sylvan Caryatids (one counter, then two). In its upkeep on turn seven, with three counters among its
# creatures and mana open, Bot1 can't cast the Ballista, which has no flash. In its main phase it casts it with X = 1 and pays the {2}
# by sacrificing the Dissident itself to Ashnod's Altar (CR 601.2g); the three counters are still removed and the Ballista resolves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Dawnhand Dissident
Forest
Mox Emerald
Sylvan Caryatid
Ashnod's Altar
Sylvan Caryatid
Forest
Walking Ballista
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

